cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GUS, please cite it as below."
title: "Gerarion Universal Standard (GUS 2.1.0): calendario computacional y proyecto de interoperabilidad temporal y evidencias verificables"
version: 2.5.0b1
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - name: "verared"
    website: "https://github.com/verared"
  - name: "Gerardo Loyola"
    website: "https://github.com/geroiloyola"
abstract: "GUS defines a regular calendar kernel (364-day common year, 371-day Gran Tempalum year) plus a continuous instant scale and an optional notary anchoring layer with post-quantum signatures (SLH-DSA / FIPS 205). Three independent implementations (Python, JavaScript, C) conform to a single normative vector set."
keywords:
  - calendar
  - timestamp
  - post-quantum
  - cryptography
  - time
repository-code: "https://github.com/verared/gerarion"
